Marketing Channels for Oilseeds 
 Marketing channels for oilseeds are different from those for foodgrains, mainly  because the extraction of oil from oilseeds is an important marketing function of  oilseeds. The flow c hart in Fig.5.2 reveals the movement of oilseeds from producers to  consumers in India. 
 The most common marketing channels for oilseeds in India are: 
(i) Producer to consumer (who either directly consumes the oilseeds or gets it  processed on custom basis); 
(ii) Producer to village trader to processor to oil retailer to consumer; 
(iii) Producer to oilseed wholesaler to processor to oil wholesaler to oil retailer to oil  consumer; 
(iv) Producer to village trader to processor to oil consumer; 
(v) Producer to government agency to processor to oil wholesaler to oil retailer to  oil consumer. 
